  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Passing in two lines",
  "description": "Two lines face each other. The first player in one line passes to the first in the other, then runs across and joins the back of that line. The receiver passes back to the next player in the first line and runs across, and so on.\n\nRun out to the right so you do not collide. It works well as a quick warm-up before a match. A spare player can warm up the goalkeeper at the same time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the floor to the receiver's blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Firm passes, but not shots."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Run straight after your pass to keep the tempo up."
    }
  ],
